The version 1.0 of the sound driver is available at nic.funet.fi
(pub/OS/Linux/xtra/snd-kit). I have upload it to tsx-11.mit.edu also and
it should be visible soon (try pub/linux/packages/sound). This version
supports AdLib, SB, SB Pro and ProAudioSpectrum16.
It works also with some SB compatible cards such as
ThunderBoard and Ati Stereo F/X.
???????SoundBlaster 16 is a big question??????????


**** Version 1.0 requires Linux 0.99.4 or later ****

Changes from version 0.5
------------------------

- Bass and treble mixer settings for PAS16 work now.
- Fixed a bug in the FM -synthesizer driver. This bug caused a
  low frequence voice when a note was switched off.
- There is a configuration program for the driver. It is now possible to
  leave out some parts of the driver.

Files
-----

There is three new files in this directory:

	snd-driv-1.0.tar.Z		The kernel Device Driver
	linux-0.99.5.sound.diff		A patch for the kernel.
					(Should work with 0.99.4 and
					0.99.5)
	snd-util-1.0.tar.Z		Several supporting programs
					and utilities. (Midi and .mod
					-players etc).

You need also one file from the earlier version:

	snd-data-0.1.tar.Z		Misc data files


Getting started
---------------

- Unarchive the snd-driv-1.0.tar.Z
- Apply the patch in linux-0.99.5.sound.diff
  (This patch changes the "make config" procedure of Linux to
  support the new sound driver).
- Perform "make config", "make clean" and "make dep"
- Recompile the kernel.

NOTE!	Install the Linux kernel sources before unarchiving the
	snd-driv-1.0.tar.Z.


